Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||10-13-2000||09:30 AM||||Heya guys and gals, started putting everything back on the new 3.2 last night. everything went smooth except for my buddy putting the valve covers on the wrong sides (he was thinking FWD engine, oil fill should be in the front...) and now, I've got all the big parts on, but I have a few mystery holes and one mystery stud. I was just wondering if someone has a chance they could look at a few little spots on an assembled engine. <BR>Holes:<BR>1. Front of outboard head, the top bolt hole that is just about the level part of the altinator bracket.<BR>2. back of outboard head, hole closest to distributer<BR>3. back of inboard head, hole closest to dist<BR>4. hole at the top of the waterpump/timing chain cover, whole is only about 1 inch deep.<P>also, I can't remeber how the belts are suposed to line up, but the alt and crank pully are lined up correctly, but the water pump is an inch or 2 beyond the crank pully, and I can't remember how it's supoes to line up, I still have to get the AC on, but it stille doesn't look like it's making scence. could this be the wrong crank pully? (shoud it have 2 pullies on it?) or am I missing something?<P>but other then all that, everything is looking good. Thanks for the help!||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-13-2000||11:25 AM||||there are engine mounting/pulling/install brackets that the factory installs that might be what the hols in the head are for.. my cars had those brackets but lost them quick (useless weight) and that left hols in the head.. no leaks! uum the belt.. i'll have to look on the car to help.. i'm way more familiar with the othe side of the motr.. sorry.. i think is wp/ alt and crank #2 is ac and crank. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
